msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I am interested in gems. "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "sell gems "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I am interested in gems. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:3640"
msgid "I'm sorry but all my wares are at my shop. Please come by there a little later. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "buy gems "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "buy gems "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I am interested in purchasing clothing. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:3813"
msgid "I have many things in my shop. Please come by there when I am open for business. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I am interested in purchasing clothing. "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 0412:38BE"
msgid "Hello, {name}, - sob- I am afraid I am not good company at this terrible time."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why do you cry? "
msgctxt "bark 0412:39F7"
msgid "I'm sorry if my tears upset you, but -sob- it is so sad. I was once the wife of Toran. But now he is gone and my son is gone...whatever shall I do? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why do you cry? "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "Where is your son? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Toran was your husband? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "Toran was your husband? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Toran was your husband? "
msgctxt "bark 0412:3AD0"
msgid "Yes and he was executed by the Tempest, Lady Mordea. -sob-. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Toran was your husband? "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "Why was he executed? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why was he executed? "
msgctxt "bark 0412:3C01"
msgid "I tried to warn him about speaking his mind so openly, but he would laugh and say that no man need fear the truth. In the end 'twas Mordea's wrath that he should have feared. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why was he executed? "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "He was an outspoken man? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Feared Mordea's wrath? "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "Feared Mordea's wrath? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Feared Mordea's wrath? "
msgctxt "bark 0412:3D3D"
msgid "She does not take kindly to things said about her. It will cost you your life, as it did my poor Toran, -sob- but I should not burden you with my troubles. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He was an outspoken man? "
msgctxt "bark 0412:3E8B"
msgid "Toran feared no one, not even the Tempest. Of late, he had begun to question the need for these executions. He was in the tavern when the guards came for him... oh, I tried to warn him, -sob-  Now I have no one, not even my son. -sob-. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where is your son? " or "Tell me again of your son. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:3F89"
msgid "My son, Torwin, left home to become a Theurgist. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where is your son? " or "Tell me again of your son. "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "What is a Theurgist? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is a Theurgist? "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 0412:4116"
msgid "A Theurgist is a healer. Oh, please do not misunderstand me, friend {name}, I think it is grand that my son should want to be a healer. Why I'm thrilled, but I am concerned by the suddenness of his decision."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What is a Theurgist? "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "You question his decision? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You question his decision? "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4329"
msgid "I'm sorry if I appear to be a terrible mother by questioning his decision, but he never showed any sign of wanting to be a healer when he was growing up. He just wanted to be a gemcutter like his father. -sob- And now that he is gone, I am left alone with no one to support me. But, at least I know he is alive and well. -sniffle- I can always hope he will return to his poor widowed mother. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You question his decision? "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "I've met your son. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You question his decision? "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "I hope he returns to you. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I hope he returns to you. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:44A8"
msgid "That would be wonderful. Oh, how I'd love to see him again. Even...even if just for a short visit. -sob-, Oh, to see his face again! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I've met your son. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:45EF"
msgid "Oh, is he well? Does he speak of me? I am sure he must be the finest healer on Argentrock. Oh, -sob- his father would be so proud... if only my husband could hear this, but he never will. He will never know... oh, no, no, no! -sob- "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I'm sorry, but your son won't be back. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4666"
msgid "What?! What do you mean?! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I'm sorry, but your son won't be back. "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "Your son had an accident. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son committed suicide. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "Your son committed suicide. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son committed suicide. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:47CF"
msgid "But..but, that can't be true, oh no, no, no, it just can't be. Oh my son, my little boy.... How can this be? -sob-, please tell me! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son committed suicide. "
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "He couldn't pass the Theurgists tests. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not know. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "I do not know. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I do not know. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4944"
msgid "Oh, I don't think I can bear it. My heart will break in two. -sob- I'm sorry, I fear I can speak no more of it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You son passed away. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "You son passed away. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You son passed away. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4A32"
msgid "He passed away? He was so young! Oh my, I can't believe it, I just can't.-sob- He mustn't be dead. No, no, no, he mustn't. I can't go on! Oh, no,no,no. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son had an accident. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4B1A"
msgid "An accident? No, I should never have let him go. Oh, now I am alone forever. What ever shall I do? What ever shall I do? No, no, no, no..... "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He was trying to resurrect his father. "
#. answer compared by the conversation code
msgctxt "ask 0412"
msgid "He was trying to resurrect his father. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He was trying to resurrect his father. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4BFE"
msgid "Oh, -sob- my brave, sweet boy.-sob- He loved his father so. Now they are both lost to me, what shall I do? What shall I do? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He couldn't pass the Theurgists tests. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4CFD"
msgid "I don't believe you! My boy is so smart. He could not have failed! -sob- He could have done it...now he does not have a chance to try again...oh no... "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He couldn't pass the Theurgists tests. "
msgctxt "bark 0412:4D47"
msgid "Perhaps we shall speak later. "
msgstr ""

